/* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   tehfiz-ornament.js — TehfizOrnament — o1
   Loaded by both apps from /app/shared/tehfiz-ornament.js?v=o1.
   GENERATED — do not edit by hand; regenerate from the ornament scripts.

   The Islimi illumination for the mushaf page: an arabesque vine border
   between a bead row and a twisted rope, petal-rosette corners, vine
   cartouches for surah titles, and a shamsa (sunburst medallion) for the
   opening pages. It is drawn once, here, as one hidden SVG sprite; every
   page shows it with <use>, so a page costs a handful of elements however
   detailed the art is.

   Why one drawing fits every page: the page body's width and its 15-line
   height both scale with the body font, so its shape never changes. The
   frame is drawn in the units of the reference page (584 x 1085.5) and each
   page's <svg viewBox> maps those units onto the body at whatever zoom.

   Colours come from CSS (tehfiz-shared.css, .tzo-* classes): --frame,
   --frame-tint, the page colour and a mid-tone between them — so themes and
   light/dark both follow without touching this file.

   Interface: TehfizOrnament.frameSvg(), .cartSvg(), .shamsaSvg() return the
   per-page markup; the sprite is injected once on load.
   ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */
